	"web_text": "The Turkmen of Central Asia use five main stitch types for their embroideries, including chain stitches known as ilme or ildirme. As found on this cap, Turkmen chain stitches are distinguished by their rounded shape, and for being worked so tightly, often in paired lines, that their ground fabric is not visible.",
